      "text": "Very well done video. Cambodia shares the same genes  as generally all South East Asian communities.  Where a religion is a combo of Buddhism fused with Taoism and a tint of other religions.  Religious customs and events are celebrated with vigour but not necessarily with the deadpan seriousness and 'follow or be chastised' attitude fear. You are not  judged by how religious you portray.  How dogmatic one project when practicing their religious habits and rituals does not reflect on their degree of devotion. Most importantly, you are not condemn for the lack of it.  It just shows how habitual it is without much questioning or thought. I personally notice in societies where religion is extremely revered and practices followed to a tee, discontent and disagreement follows.",
